# Test fixtures are byte-exact by design.
#
# tests/sample_files.rs asserts the exact line endings and encoding it finds on
# disk, so git must not rewrite them. Windows checkouts default to
# core.autocrlf=true, which turned report.sql's LF into CRLF and made a correct
# detector look wrong on the Windows runner.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in BOTH directions, which is what
# these files need: report.sql must stay LF *and* crlf.sql must stay CRLF.
# `text eol=lf` would fix the first by breaking the second.
dev/samples/* -text
